REASON","end":true,"content":"With the emulator running, I'm moving on to the data layer design. I'm planning to add ClassicPoemDetailPage into the classicpoem module alongside ClassicPoemView, using readClassicPoem(id) and registering it in the route map, while the sentence module gets a lightweight existsClassicPoem(id) check via a simple select query to confirm a poem exists before proceeding.\n\nI'm also setting up the sentence module's routing with SentenceIndexPage, SentenceBookmarksPage, and SentenceDetailPage, plus the data functions readSentence(id) and readRandomSentenceExcept(id) with a fallback to the current sentence when there's only one row. I'm handling poem_id null checks carefully, treating zero as null too, and designing the bookmark operations—check-then-insert for adding, straightforward delete for removing, and a join query to pull all bookmarked sentences ordered by most recent. Now I'm deciding whether to house the bookmark functions in a new SentenceBookmark.ets file or fold them into Sentence.ets, leaning toward a separate file.\n\nI'll just use literal Chinese strings for the UI text and show success toasts via the prompt action API. For navigation, I'll pass the sentence ID as a route param and retrieve it in the destination page's onReady callback, casting it from the path info parameter.\n\nI'm fairly confident newer docs pass name and param to the builder, and loading data in onReady should work fine even with ComponentV2's @Local state.\n\nFor preventing double-push on fast clicks, I'm thinking of checking the current top of the page stack before pushing again—using getAllPathName() to see if the target page is already there and skipping the push if so.\n\nI'm thinking a cleaner approach is a generic guard helper that only pushes a new page if the current top of the stack matches the expected source page name, rather than scattering size checks everywhere. I'm also considering whether NavPathStack's launch mode options could handle this more directly instead of a manual check.\n\nI need to handle re-entrancy for bookmark toggling and refresh with busy/loading flags, so rapid taps just get ignored during an in-flight operation rather than causing crashes or inconsistent state. For the index page's onShown lifecycle, I should re-query the bookmark state to stay in sync when returning to the page.\n\n","startTime":1792250983445,"lastModifiedTime":1792251006090},{"id":"toolu_bdrk_012X3H7QW2UGEDFxRKvYhvd4","type":"TOOL","toolName":"update_task","params":{"status":"completed","taskId":"1"},"toolState":"executed","result":{"output":"Updated task #1 status","metadata":{"taskId":"1","updatedFields":["status"],"statusChange":{"from":"in_progress","to":"completed"},"ignoredDependencyIds":[],"taskSnapshot":{"$blob":"sha256:feb62026556b4b2b4878d497277191534774e095977d82fdcc9ae37709ffabe4","version":1,"encoding":"json","byteLength":1111,"compression":"none"}}}},{"id":"toolu_bdrk_015Wo1tHPfTQvnqiUSkDNaQa","type":"TOOL","toolName":"update_task","params":{"status":"in_progress","taskId":"2"},"toolState":"executed","result":{"output":"Updated task #2 status","metadata":{"taskId":"2","updatedFields":["status"],"statusChange":{"from":"pending","to":"in_progress"},"ignoredDependencyIds":[],"taskSnapshot":{"$blob":"sha256:2344539034483828a7fec87c53e60112b180616e8ec9f7ca24038441f44cacb4","version":1,"encoding":"json","byteLength":1115,"compression":"none"}}}},{"id":"toolu_bdrk_01RAfUHZd4G8rSv1aDtJ4VXt","type":"TOOL","toolName":"edit_file","params":{"file_path":"/Users/bress/Documents/code/harmonycup-work/jm-spec75/commons/constants/src/main/ets/DbConst.ets","old_string":{"$blob":"sha256:9d8fcaa1bd2b9ffc2b46f23193547eba35aed32d017bccb63769cc21dc749d71","version":1,"encoding":"utf8","byteLength":277,"compression":"none"},"new_string":{"$blob":"sha256:3f2fd5d71528a29857d00582cf0325e4d15656eddb1bbd442c57e1500f3c0fa0","version":1,"encoding":"utf8","byteLength":1369,"compression":"none"}},"toolState":"executed","result":{"o