rase imported content, so I need to do it through the UI — open the bookmarks list, repeatedly open the first item and unbookmark it until the list is empty.\n\nNow I'm sketching out the first test scenario covering the home screen and toolbar: verifying entry from home navigates to the sentence index page with populated content, checking the four toolbar buttons appear with correct text and order, confirming refresh produces different content/source pairs across five clicks, and checking that re-entering the page gives random...\n\n...content with at least two distinct results, that backing out restores the home menu, that rapid double-clicking the home entry only requires one back press, that generating an image opens a preview with the same content underneath, that rapid refresh taps don't crash, and that the classic poems entry point still works as a regression check.\n\nThen I'm planning the bookmarking test file: starting with a cleanup step, verifying the bookmark toggle label switches to \"已收藏\" after clicking, checking the bookmarks list page shows the saved item and that returning to the index preserves the bookmarked state, verifying bookmark ordering when adding a second item, and checking that clicking a bookmarked item opens its detail view.\n\nNow I'm continuing the bookmark detail flow — matching the detail page title and content against the index, confirming the detail view shows \"已收藏\" and backing out returns to the list correctly. I'm also outlining tests for unbookmarking from the detail view (label reverts and item disappears from the list), unbookmarking from the index, handling rapid double-taps on bookmarking without creating duplicate entries, verifying the bookmark label stays correct after a refresh, checking persistence across an app restart, and confirming the empty-list message appears after clearing all bookmarks.\n\nFor the fourth test scenario, I'm working out how to build a mapping from sentence content and source to poem IDs using